ctions.empty.noCollectionsTitle":"Create your first collection","component.myCollections.empty.noCollectionsDesc":"Collect related stories together in one place for easy viewing and sharing","component.myCollections.empty.noCollectionsBtn":"Create new collection","component.myCollections.empty.noFavesTitle":"Your favorite collections will appear here","component.myCollections.empty.noFavesDesc":"All of your favorite collections will live here for quick and easy access","component.myCollections.builder.add":"Add to collection","component.myCollections.builder.empty":"This collection is empty","component.myCollections.builder.fullMessage":"Collections can include up to 60 items. You’ll need to remove some before you can add any new ones.","component.myCollections.builder.removeCollection":"Remove from collection","component.collections.builder.hideCollectionItem":"Hide item","component.collections.builder.showCollectionItem":"Show item","component.myCollections.builder.editDetails":"Edit details","component.myStories.index.quickStart.explorerMapTour.title":"Explorer map tour","component.myStories.index.quickStart.explorerMapTour.description":"Readers explore a curated set of places in whatever order they choose","component.myStories.index.quickStart.explorerMapTour.alt":"An explorer map tour with a list of places on one side and a map of those locations on the other","component.myContent.allContent":"All content","component.myContent.allStatuses":"All statuses","component.myContent.viewItemsIn":"View items in","component.myContent.contentType":"Content type","component.myContent.publishStatus":"Publish status","component.myContent.filters":"Filters","component.myContent.allSharing":"All sharing","component.myContent.sort":"Sort","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p1.title":"What is ArcGIS StoryMaps?","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p1.content.first":"ArcGIS StoryMaps is the next-generation multimedia storytelling tool that enables you to combine maps and apps with a variety of media to tell a story. It offers four content formats built for different purposes: stories, briefings, frames, and collections. Additionally, themes and templates capture your design and storytelling patterns to help you create new, high-quality content quickly.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p1.content.second":"Click through this short tutorial to learn about each type of item you can create with ArcGIS StoryMaps.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p1.content.third":"Explore examples of all content types in the \u003clink\u003eArcGIS StoryMaps gallery\u003c/link\u003e","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p2.content.first":"Stories are narratives that look and behave like an article or blog. They can feature immersive sections, which are media-centric, interactive viewing experiences. You can choreograph the movement of maps and media in an immersive section to create an engaging experience for readers.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p2.content.second":"All types of StoryMaps are created using an intuitive builder that makes it easy to integrate media, maps, apps, and content from the web. You can even create simple maps directly in the builder to highlight locations of interest.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p3.content.first":"Briefings are a slide-based format designed for delivering live presentations and succinct information sharing. You build briefing slides using flexible content blocks to add maps, apps, and media.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p3.content.second":"A briefing can be shared as a web link or viewed through the ArcGIS StoryMaps Briefings app. The briefings app is especially useful for executives and field workers who need offline access to briefings when they don’t have a reliable connection.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p4.content":"Frames are a mobile-first output ideal for shorter-form storytelling and information sharing. Common uses for frames include a promotional teaser, event announcement, or hand-held digital tour. They are designed to be viewed on phones and shared on social media platforms for greater reach.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p5.content.first":"Collections are a set of related content assembled in a portfolio-like viewing experience. You can add stories, briefings, and frames to a collection and include supporting content like apps, PDFs, and media. A collection can also present items on a map for geographic exploration.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p5.content.second":"You can use collections to group stories around a topic or share content with a specific audience. Put a collection on autoplay at a conference or on a lobby display monitor to attract attendees or show off your organization’s work.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p6.content.first":"Themes capture the look and feel of your content. You define colors, fonts, and styles for elements such as buttons, quotes, and section separators. Once you’ve built a custom theme, you can apply it to any content you’ve created with ArcGIS StoryMaps.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p6.content.second":"If you’re looking for inspiration, an AI assistant can generate suggested starting points for a new theme based on a description or image, or you can simply choose from a selection of ready-to-use, professionally designed themes.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p7.content.first":"Templates are a special kind of story that others can copy and build upon. They can be used to serve as a starting point for periodic reports, class assignments, or a set of similar stories about different places.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p7.content.second":"The template builder is identical to the story builder, with the addition of an Instructions block that allows you to provide directions to anyone building upon that template. You can build a template from scratch or create a template version of a story you’ve already put together.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p8.title":"Learn more and get inspired","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p8.content.first":"Visit the \u003clink\u003eArcGIS StoryMaps blog\u003c/link\u003e to learn the basics of storytelling and tips to make your content more effective and engaging.","common.createDropdown.onboarding.modal.p8.content.second":"Also be sure to explore the \u003clink\u003eArcGIS StoryMaps gallery\u003c/link\u003e. It is a great place to get inspired by many exemplary examples of stories, briefings, frames, collections, templates, and themes created by the vibrant, diverse storytelling community.","common.banner.storyMapperContest.shortTitle":"Enter the 2026 ArcGIS StoryMaps Competition","common.banner.storyMapperContest.description":"Show how maps make your community better. Submit your story by December 11.","component.socialSharing.linkSuccess":"Success","component.storyCreator.creating":"Launching story builder","component.briefingCreator.creating":"Launching briefing builder","component.storyEditor.saveErrorTitle":"Sorry!","component.storyEditor.saveErrorDetails":"There was a problem saving your story","component.themeCreator.launchingThemeBuilder":"Launching theme builder","component.theme.confirmDelete.alt":"Are you sure you want to delete this theme? This cannot be undone.","component.themes.empty.noThemesTitle":"Create your first theme","component.themes.empty.noThemesDesc":"Capture a set of fonts, colors, and styles to reuse and share with others","component.themes.empty.noFavesTitle":"Your favorite themes will appear here","component.themes.empty.noFavesDesc":"All of your favorite themes will live here for quick and easy access","component.themes.index.searchLabel":"Search themes","component.themes.themes":"Themes","component.themes.themes.beta":"Themes (beta)","component.themes.itemCard.title":"Theme (Untitled)","component.themes.myThemes":"My Themes","component.themes.confirmDelete.button":"Delete theme 